# Review: Hello Worker

This spec is seed content for the Hello Worker sample space, not a description of code in the repo. The
template (`WorkerSpace.ts`) stores it as a `Spec` object, and the agent working the space is meant to
write and deploy the Worker it describes at run time (D-1). No Worker source exists in the repository:
no fetch handler, no `Greeting` type and no `wrangler` config under `src/samples/worker/` or elsewhere.
`WorkerSpace.test.ts` checks the seeded objects, and the `hello-worker-diagram` eval grades only the
architecture drawing. Every item is therefore `missing`, which is the intended state of this spec.
Of 4 items: 0 done, 0 untested, 0 partial, 0 diverged, 4 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict Greeting: No Greeting type exists; the agent is meant to write it with the Worker.
  status: missing
  note: Searched `src/samples/worker/` and the repo for a Worker answering with `message` and `time`; the sample holds only seed objects (`tasks.ts`, `project.ts`, `spec.ts`, `features.ts`).
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.1: No fetch handler exists in the repo; it is the run's output, not checked-in code.
